# CKB Rust

Toolchain, molecule, binary size, and `make build` / `make test` live in `nervlith-contract/AGENTS.md`. Follow that file. Do not restate it here.

## Shape

Keep `main` thin: load the script group, dispatch, return. Put errors, molecule types, and validation in their own modules (`error.rs`, `types`, `validate`). One check per function.

Prefer `ckb_std::high_level` and `ckb-types`. Drop to raw syscalls only when high-level cannot express the read.

## Comments

Explain the cell-model reason: which cells, which witness slot, and what a missing input means. Do not restate the syntax.

```rust
// BAD: read the first input
let input = load_cell(0, Source::Input)?;

// GOOD: the membership lock only unlocks when the fee xUDT
// is an input. A missing type match means the spender is not a member.
let membership = find_xudt(args.token_hash, Source::Input)?;
```
